"followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-20T16:21:52Z","updated_at":"2025-08-20T16:29:22Z","body":"@KoBeWi \r\n> If someone adds a new node with a resource, but does not mark embed,\r\n\r\nAssuming you are talking about VisualShaderNodeCustom - VisualShaderNodeCustom cannot have Resource Embeds, nothing in the [current API](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/4.4/classes/class_visualshadernodecustom.html#class-visualshadernodecustom-private-method-get-property-name) provides that functionality unless I am misunderstanding. \r\n\r\n@QbieShay \r\n> Came back to this. I wonder how we feel about adding a hint_default(\"res://blabla.png\") ?\r\n\r\nWe talked about this in the Rendering Meeting today (Aug.20) (You were there :) ) and determined hint_default is not a workable feature.\r\n\r\nConclusion we reached in the Rendering Meeting for the issue is to throw a warning popup when the conversion plugin is called via Editor, and fall back to throwing an Error (like the current solution) when the conversion is initiated via code. I will adjust my fix to throw the popup when I have some spare time","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3207079306/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3207498861","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109375#issuecomment-3207498861","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109375","id":3207498861,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6_Loxt","user":{"login":"KoBeWi","id":2223172,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMjMxNzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2223172?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi","html_url":"https://github.com/KoBeWi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-20T17:58:41Z","updated_at":"2025-08-20T17:58:41Z","body":"> Assuming you are talking about VisualShaderNodeCustom\r\n\r\nNo, adding a new visual shader node type in the engine. This PR modifies many classes, and in the future there may be more classes that will need similar checks.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3207498861/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3207612486","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109375#issuecomment-3207612486","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109375","id":3207612486,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6_MEhG","user":{"login":"ColinSORourke","id":44822820,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0ODIyODIw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44822820?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke","html_url":"https://github.com/ColinSORourke","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-20T18:40:09Z","updated_at":"2025-08-20T18:40:09Z","body":"> The problem with this solution is that VisualShader nodes have to count the embeds manually. If someone adds a new node with a resource, but does not mark embed, it will miss the error.\r\n> No, adding a new visual shader node type in the engine. This PR modifies many classes, and in the future there may be more classes that will need similar checks.\r\n\r\nTracking embeds is necessary to catch and communicate this bad conversion behavior. I think the responsibility of tracking embeds is best assigned to individual node classes. Currently only 6 VisualShaderNode classes can have embedded resources, and I would say safe handling of resources on future node classes is important, and low cost.\r\n\r\nI have a hard time envisioning an alternative architecture that defers the responsibility of tracking embeds somewhere else? Managing this information from the Visual Shader Editor Plugin seems like it would require more work than having each node track itself, and I don't know if the Visual Shader resource Class has enough info to do any of this tracking.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3207612486/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3250008507","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109375#issuecomment-3250008507","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109375","id":3250008507,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7BtzG7","user":{"login":"ColinSORourke","id":44822820,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0ODIyODIw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44822820?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke","html_url":"https://github.com/ColinSORourke","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-03T16:49:09Z","updated_at":"2025-09-03T16:49:09Z","body":"@KoBeWi Talked about it in the rendering meeting today, and have updated the PR with a different architecture for the fix. \r\n\r\n```\r\n// Returns 0 if no embeds, 1 if external embeds, 2 if builtin embeds\r\nint VisualShader::has_node_embeds() const {\r\n\tbool external_embeds = false;\r\n\tfor (int i = 0; i < TYPE_MAX; i++) {\r\n\t\tfor (const KeyValue<int, Node> &E : graph[i].nodes) {\r\n\t\t\tList<PropertyInfo> props;\r\n\t\t\tE.value.node->get_property_list(&props);\r\n\t\t\t// For classes that inherit from VisualShaderNode, the class properties start at the 12th, and the last value is always 'script'\r\n\t\t\tfor (int i = 12; i < props.size() - 1; i++) {\r\n\t\t\t\t// VisualShaderNodeCustom cannot have embeds\r\n\t\t\t\tif (props.get(i).name == \"VisualShaderNodeCustom\") {\r\n\t\t\t\t\tbreak;\r\n\t\t\t\t}\r\n\t\t\t\t// Ref<Resource> properties get classed as type Variant::Object\r\n\t\t\t\tif (props.get(i).type == Variant::OBJECT) {\r\n\t\t\t\t\tRef<Resource> res = E.value.node->get(props.get(i).name);\r\n\t\t\t\t\tif (res.is_valid()) {\r\n\t\t\t\t\t\tif (res->is_built_in()) {\r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\treturn 2;\r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t} else {\r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\texternal_embeds = true;\r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t}\r\n\t\t\t\t\t}\r\n\t\t\t\t}\r\n\t\t\t}\r\n\t\t}\r\n\t}\r\n\r\n\treturn external_embeds;\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis single function in the VisualShader class should be able to catch which child nodes have embedded resource properties without requiring any overhead on the VisualShaderNode classes","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3250008507/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3263998778","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109375#issuecomment-3263998778","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/r